Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Read the number of mining sites and candidate connections.
3. Create a weighted adjacency matrix to represent the mining network.
4. Initialize the key values to infinity, parent values to -1, and all vertices as unvisited.
5. Set the key value of the starting vertex to zero.
6. Select the unvisited vertex with the minimum key value.
7. Mark the selected vertex as visited.
8. If the selected vertex has a parent, display the edge, its weight, and the updated running total cost.
9. Update the key and parent values of adjacent unvisited vertices whenever a lower-cost connection is found.
10. Repeat the process until all vertices are visited or no further connection is possible.
11. Check whether the number of selected edges equals \(V-1\). If yes, display the minimum total network cost; otherwise, report that the graph is disconnected.
12. Ask the user whether an edge weight should be updated.
13. If the user chooses yes, read the two site numbers and the new edge weight.
14. Update the edge weight in the adjacency matrix and apply Prim’s Algorithm again.
15. Repeat the update process if requested.
16. Stop the program.
